<div class="card">
    <div class="card-header bg-warning text-dark">
        <h3 class="mb-0">Tab 3 - Third Content</h3>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
        <h5 class="card-title">Third tab loaded!</h5>
        <p class="card-text">
            This is the third example of dynamically loaded content. All transitions happen without page reload and without changing the browser address.
        </p>
        <div class="alert alert-success">
            <strong>Success!</strong> Content loaded dynamically via view-box.
        </div>
        <div class="alert alert-info">
            <strong>Difference:</strong> This content is loaded from a View file (<code>Tab3.cshtml</code>), unlike Tab1 which returns text content directly from the controller.
        </div>
        <div class="alert alert-warning">
            <strong>Important!</strong> The browser address remained the same thanks to the <code>changing-browser-address-enable="false"</code> parameter.
        </div>

        <div class="alert alert-secondary">
            <h5><strong>JavaScript Implementation Details:</strong></h5>
            <p>This tab is loaded not through the standard <code>&lt;view-box-link&gt;</code>, but through a regular HTML element with JavaScript event handler.</p>
            <p><strong>When to use the JS variant:</strong></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Full control over appearance and behavior of the control element is needed</li>
                <li>Integration with existing JavaScript frameworks (React, Vue, Angular) is required</li>
                <li>Additional logic before sending request is needed (validation, confirmation)</li>
                <li>Content loading should happen programmatically from any code location</li>
                <li>Control element is not a link (buttons, forms, custom components)</li>
            </ul>
            <p><strong>Implementation Example:</strong></p>
            <pre><code>&lt;div id="dynamic-tab3-link"
    class="btn btn-primary"
    onclick="ViewBoxRegistry.sendRequest('dynamic-content-box', '/DynamicContent/Tab3');"&gt;
    Test request from JS
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
            <p><strong>Main API Methods:</strong></p>
            <ul>
                <li><code>ViewBoxRegistry.sendRequest(viewBoxId, uri)</code> - send request</li>
                <li><code>ViewBoxRegistry.abortCurrentRequest(viewBoxId)</code> - cancel current request</li>
            </ul>
            <p><strong>Method Parameters:</strong></p>
            <ul>
                <li><code>viewBoxId</code> - ID of target view-box element</li>
                <li><code>uri</code> - address for content loading</li>
            </ul>
            <p><strong>Additional Features:</strong></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Automatic cancellation of previous request when sending new one</li>
                <li>Support for passing additional parameters in POST requests</li>
                <li>Programmatic cancellation of running request via <code>ViewBoxRegistry.abortCurrentRequest(viewBoxId)</code></li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

